    "done_when": "reckon/crew/ticker.py renders each row, left to right, as: time; a one-character attention column reading ! exactly for new states that owe the coordinator something (blocked, stalled, abandoned, failed, needs-help, a completion awaiting promotion or review) and blank otherwise; model; effort; role; node name truncated to keep at least two spaces before the next cell; the transition as the previous state right-aligned to the widest state word, a single → in one fixed column on every row, and the new state left-aligned; elapsed right-aligned in one format; the w b u q counter block; the plain reason clause; no action word (resume, recover, investigate, repair, inspect, promote, review, observe) is printed anywhere between the transition and the elapsed cell; the previous state printed is the state this Ticker last rendered for that run, falling back to the event's from_state only for a run it has never rendered, and a row whose new state equals that last rendered state is not printed; the ledger_row withdrawn branch is removed and the producer's withdrawn state is rendered as given; tests/test_ticker_row_is_one_transition.py holds a property test over every (previous, new) state pair the classifier emits including none-to-state, node names at, over and under the name width, elapsed 0 s to 30 h, with and without a queued run, asserting after stripping ANSI that the arrow and the attention, elapsed, counter and reason columns each start at one column on every row and every cell boundary has at least two spaces; a chain test feeding the pair dispatched to abandoned then dispatched to working asserts the second row prints abandoned → working; a same-state test asserts one row for repeated same-state events; the lead's rows are fixtures (dispatched → abandoned with ! and no trailing verb, dispatched → working with a blank attention column, names review-of-hook-stop-mode-silent-without-follower and review-of-obligations-are-a-derived-view keep their gutter); four declared mutations are applied and each observed to fail with its own log: print the action word after the transition, drop the two-space name gap, take the previous state from the event's from_state, print same-state rows; every listed ticker, watch and recovery test file passes at the committed head with the absolute .venv interpreter, with any assertion that pinned the old geometry updated and named in the manifest; reckon/cli.py is not edited, and carrying the Ticker's last-rendered state across a re-arm is reported in follow_ons for the follower node; ruff reports no more findings than at base on the edited files",
